-reports/
---------
-
-Under the `admin/` directory, ``reports/`` directory exists.  This directory is
-for setup of DAMON report system (queues and triggers).
-
-In the directory, ``state`` file exists.  Reading it returns the current state
-of the report system.  Reading ``on`` means queus are setup and triggers are
-running.  Reading ``off`` means triggers are not running and queues are
-destructed.  Writing ``on`` to the file makes DAMON to construct the queues and
-make triggers run.  Writing ``off`` to the file makes triggers stop running and
-the queues are destructed.  Writing ``commit`` to the file updates the internal
-state while keeping previous state as much as possible.  For example, reports
-on queues are preserved as long as the config for the queue is same to before.
-
-reports/queues/
----------------
-
-Under ``reports`` directory, ``queues`` directory exists.  This directory is
-for setup of DAMON report queues.  Under the `queues` directory, ``nr_queues``
-file exists.  Writing a number of the file creates the number of directories,
-named ``0`` to ``N-1``.  It also informs the user wants that number of report
-queues for next ``commit`` or ``on`` writes to the ``reports/state`` file.
-
-Under the each number-named directory, ``size`` file exists.  writing an
-unsigned integer to the file sets the size of the queue.  Reading the file
-shows the last successful input to the file.
-
-reports/triggers/
------------------
-
-Under ``reports`` directory, ``triggers`` directory exists.  The directory is
-for setup of DAMON report triggers.  Under the `triggers`` directory,
-``nr_triggers`` file exists.  Writing a number of the file creates the number
-of directories, named ``0`` to ``N-1``.  It also informs the user wants that
-number of report triggers to run for next ``commit`` or ``on`` writes to the
-``reports/state`` file.
-
-Under the each number-named directory, ``report_type`` file exists.  The type
-of reports the trigger should generate can be written to the file.  Reading the
-file shows the last successfult input to the file.
-
-Under the directory, ``queues`` file exists.  Indices of report queues the
-trigger should put the reports to should be written to the file, using ``,`` as
-the delimiter between indices.
-
