@@ -826,6 +775,28 @@ Please note that it's highly recommended to use user space tools like `damo
 <https://github.com/damonitor/damo>`_ rather than manually reading and writing
 the files as above.  Above is only for an example.
 
+reports/producers/
+------------------
+
+Under the `admin/` directory, ``reports/producers`` directory exists.  This
+directory is for configuring DAMON report producers.
+
+In the directory, ``state`` file exists.  Writing ``on`` to the file let
+enabled report producers start working.  Writing ``off`` to the file stops all
+report producers and drop pre-generated reports.  Reading the file shows ``on``
+or ``off`` if any or no producer is running, repsectively.
+
+reports/producers/<type>/
+-------------------------
+
+For each DAMON-supported report ``<type>``, ``<type>`` directory exists under
+``producers`` directory.
+
+Under the ``<type>`` directory, ``enabled`` file exists.  Writing ``Y`` or
+``N`` to the file specifies the producer should start or stop running when the
+next writes to ``producers/state`` file is done.  Reading the file shows the
+last successfully written input.
+
